  "notes": [
    "Regular -AR verb — follows standard -AR endings with no exceptions (the *ch* digraph never changes before *e*, so no spelling adjustments are needed)",
    "Past participle: *emborrachado* (regular)",
    "Transitive: means \"to get someone/something drunk\" or \"to intoxicate\" — *el vino lo emborrachó rápido* (the wine got him drunk fast)",
    "The reflexive form *emborracharse* (\"to get drunk oneself\") is far more common in everyday speech — worth adding as its own verb entry if needed",
    "Related: *borracho/a* (drunk, adj./noun), *borrachera* (drunkenness, a bender)"
